# n8n Workflow Standards

## Workflow File Organization

### Structure
- Workflows in `/n8n/workflows/` or `/n8n/demo-data/workflows/`
- Credentials in `/n8n/credentials/` or `/n8n/demo-data/credentials/`
- Supporting docs in same directory as workflows

### File Naming
- Use descriptive kebab-case filenames: `workflow-name.json`
- Avoid generic names like `workflow1.json`
- Include version if multiple variants: `price-comparison-v2.json`

## Workflow JSON Standards

### Export Method
- Always export from n8n UI (don't manually edit JSON)
- Use "Download" → "Export workflow" from n8n editor
- Maintain JSON structure integrity

### Workflow Metadata
- Include meaningful workflow name (not "My workflow")
- Add description explaining workflow purpose
- Use tags for categorization where applicable
- Set appropriate workflow settings (error workflow, timezone)

### Documentation Requirements
- Document workflow purpose in README or workflow description
- List required credentials and their setup
- Document expected inputs/outputs
- Include testing instructions

## Credential Management

### Security
- Never commit actual credential values
- Use credential placeholders/templates only
- Reference required credentials in `.env.example` or documentation
- Export credential structure only (for sharing setup)

### Credential Organization
- Group related credentials logically
- Use descriptive credential names
- Document credential requirements in workflow README

## Workflow Validation

### Before Committing
- Validate JSON syntax (`jq . workflow.json` or similar)
- Test workflow execution in n8n UI
- Verify all required credentials are documented
- Check for hardcoded values (should use expressions/variables)

### Dependencies
- Document external service requirements
- List required n8n node packages
- Specify minimum n8n version if using newer features
- Document workflow dependencies on other workflows

## n8n Node Best Practices

### Error Handling
- Use "Continue on Fail" appropriately
- Add error workflows for critical processes
- Include meaningful error messages
- Handle edge cases gracefully

### Performance
- Avoid infinite loops in workflow logic
- Use appropriate node types (avoid overuse of Function nodes)
- Implement reasonable timeouts for external calls
- Consider workflow complexity and execution time

## Integration with Docker Stack

### Service Dependencies
- Workflows requiring Ollama: document model requirements
- Workflows using Qdrant: document collection setup
- Workflows needing PostgreSQL: document schema requirements
- Reference service URLs using environment variables where possible